If Jane is not guilty, then it is quite plausible that some injuries later identified on Ben were not obvious, not yet visible, or simply not recorded when he arrived at hospital.

Reasons:
- subtle bruising or internal injuries may not be immediately apparent;
- emergency staff focus first on resuscitation, not full forensic documentation;
- some marks become clearer over time;
- absence from nursing notes is not the same as proof the injuries were absent.

So under innocence, the fact that nurses did not note the injuries does not seem very surprising.

My judgment: 71
